      "side": 1,
      "message": "But we don\u0027t seem to check for that. In fact, in ProxyTracker#fixupLinkProperties, there is a comment saying only one PAC proxy server can be up on the device which is true, but I don\u0027t think it\u0027s true that only one network can have a PAC URL in its properties ; if we fixup the properties of any network, not just the default one, we will set the port to the local proxy network for non-default networks, which will direct their HTTP traffic to the wrong proxy.\n\nISTM we should pass the network to handleProxyHasChanged (it is in the pair in l.5341) and return if it\u0027s not the default network.\n\nThings actually become more complex now that we have default networks per app...",
